          "explanation": {
            "content": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Incorrect. The statement that is NOT true is: at equilibrium, the rate of the forward reaction is greater than the rate of the reverse reaction. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "9332km8d3vh99ty",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A chemical reaction is at equilibrium when the concentrations of the reactant and product species are no longer changing over time. Because chemical equilibrium is a dynamic equilibrium, the forward and reverse reactions are still occurring with the rates of the forward and reverse reactions being equal at equilibrium."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u04cnt29mgsioux",
                "type": "p"
              }
